The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the file is on disk but not committed; the || true in the command hid that. I didn't force-add it.

The new finding is outside cli, in the provider defaults (`src/providers.rs`). OpenRouter's public model list (452 models) spells every Anthropic model id with dots, e.g. anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6, which has a 1M context and a 128000-token output limit. yoyo's OpenRouter default is anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6, with dashes, and that id isn't in the list. Every Anthropic id I tried on OpenRouter, dots or dashes, gets yoyo's guessed limits, so replies are capped at 4096 output tokens. I couldn't check whether OpenRouter rejects the dashed default outright: I have no OpenRouter key, and the auth error comes back first. I posted these facts on #1037, which already had OpenRouter as an unchecked row. Claude Code 2.1.314 fixed the same kind of bug.

Other points for the planner:
• Where to spend the self-driven slot: cli took 5 of the last 8 self-driven changes, so it should go elsewhere. The OpenRouter fix is the strongest candidate; #1100, #1102 and #1094 are alternatives.
• #1114 still reproduces: yoyo -p --print-system-prompt prints the system prompt instead of sending the text as a prompt. The ticket also says yoyo --system --yes hi turns on auto-approve, which makes it a safety issue; I didn't re-run that one.
• Last night's evolve run failed (01:12). The logs came back empty, so the cause is unknown. Running out of disk is plausible, since the creator's commit this morning fixes a disk-full failure from 10-31, but it isn't confirmed.
• Module-size gate headroom is tight: src/config.rs can grow 11 more lines and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs 14 more (it isn't in the size-gate list) before cargo test fails and the whole task reverts.
• Smaller things still broken:
  • def, find, memories and outline search for --bogus instead of refusing it (#1111).
  • yoyo memories tells shell users to use /remember (#1086).
  • docs --bogus is reported as a network failure.

The research covered Claude Code 2.1.313–2.1.316 and Codex's October releases, and is saved to yopedia. The biggest gaps are still interactive: Codex added sending a follow-up while it's still responding, and yoyo has neither that nor a TUI.
